# Repositories to place on the build VM, one per line.
#
#   <git-url> <target-dir> [branch]
#
# Format is deliberately dumb: it is read by vm-bootstrap.sh with `read -r`, so a
# comment line starting with # is all the structure it needs.
#
# These are the repos the builder actually compiles from. The catalog in
# sources-catalog.json lists upstream projects the builder can *offer*; cloning
# all 33 of them would pull hundreds of gigabytes of AOSP mirrors that the
# builder fetches on demand instead. What goes on the VM is the editor's own
# tree plus the forks the two real targets build against.
#
# Anything not listed here is still available to the pipeline: the builder clones
# it into the build root when a composition asks for it.

# The builder itself. Everything else is reached through it.
https://github.com/015stray91/ANYREALM-.git ANYREALM- main

# Kernels. These are the only two structures that ship as NUKI, and they never
# cross: zenith is x86_64 desktop, genevn is arm64 mobile.
https://github.com/015stray91/AR-NUKI-genevn.git AR-NUKI-genevn
# Branch is pinned where it is not `main`: a clone that quietly takes the wrong
# branch builds the wrong kernel and reports a source error much later.
https://github.com/015stray91/kernel-zenith.git kernel-zenith 6.12_android-x86

# Mobile Linux UX. phosh-ux + phoc + lomiri + lipstick cover every display
# owner the UX picker offers, and mobian supplies the debos recipes that build
# the arm64 rootfs.
https://github.com/015stray91/phosh-ux.git phosh-ux
https://github.com/015stray91/phoc.git phoc
https://github.com/015stray91/lomiri.git lomiri
https://github.com/015stray91/lipstick.git lipstick master
https://github.com/015stray91/mobian.git mobian master

# Root manager sources. KernelSU-Next is the default; the shared tree also
# carries the other variants the picker offers.
https://github.com/015stray91/Super-Builders.git Super-Builders 015stray91
